  Dot Popper's copy of Lota 0.2.2's Android host manifest
  (ext/lota/phone/host/android in the gem), which android.yml lays over
  Lota's host in the phone project. Its two changes: Dot Popper decides
  what Back does itself, as Escape (Shell::App), so the meta-data below
  asks SDL to trap Back; and the activity handles every configuration
  change that leaves its pixels alone, not only turning and keyboards.

  SDL can't survive its activity being made again: onDestroy quits the
  game, and the new activity's onCreate calls System.exit. So a change
  the manifest doesn't list ends the game: dark theme (uiMode), font size
  (fontScale, fontWeightAdjustment), language (locale, layoutDirection,
  grammaticalGender), a SIM (mcc, mnc), and overlays (assetsPaths), which
  Android applies when a wallpaper's colours or the system font change,
  and to a just-installed app, sometimes after its first launch has begun.
  SDL's onConfigurationChanged passes the language and dark theme on.
  Display size (density) is on the list too, though not in SDL's own
  manifest: the game keeps drawing at the density it started with, since
  LÖVE reads the dpi scale once and the window's pixels don't change, and
  takes up the new size at its next launch. Lota's notes follow.

  A Lota game's manifest, in place of the one fledge build android writes
  (Fledge's lib/fledge/templates/android/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml at
  v0.5.1), whose icon mark Fledge fills here too. It adds what
  love-android's manifest asks of the system for LÖVE's engine: OpenGL ES
  3.0, vibration, a full screen with no title bar, and no restart of the
  activity when the screen turns or a keyboard comes and goes.

  Back reaches the game as the key escape, and then SDL closes the app,
  as in LÖVE. A game that decides what Back does itself adds, inside
  <application>:

    <meta-data android:name="SDL_ENV.SDL_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON" android:value="1" />

  and MainActivity then keeps Android 13 and newer from closing the app
  through predictive back, too.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.VIBRATE" />
    <uses-feature android:glEsVersion="0x00030000" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.touchscreen" android:required="false" />
    <application android:label="@string/app_name"@@ICON@@>
        <meta-data android:name="SDL_ENV.SDL_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON" android:value="1" />
        <activity
            android:name="org.setdef.fledge.host.MainActivity"
            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen"
            android:configChanges="orientation|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|screenLayout|keyboard|keyboardHidden|navigation|uiMode|fontScale|fontWeightAdjustment|locale|layoutDirection|grammaticalGender|mcc|mnc|touchscreen|colorMode|assetsPaths|density"
            android:launchMode="singleInstance"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
